Good morning, here is your TMT Breakout newsletter for today.

The semiconductor sector continues to show strength as artificial intelligence spending accelerates across major cloud providers. The market is pricing in sustained demand growth through the second half of the year.

Key developments to watch this week include several major earnings reports and potential regulatory updates.

NVDA reported earnings that beat expectations by a wide margin, with data center revenue jumping significantly.

AAPL announced a new partnership that could expand its services revenue stream in emerging markets.

MSFT Azure growth reaccelerated, beating consensus estimates as enterprise AI adoption picks up.

TSLA deliveries came in below expectations, raising questions about demand in the EV market.

AMD gained share in the server CPU market, with EPYC processors seeing strong enterprise adoption.

